| 3200 | Treasury stock | contra-equity |

### S-corp (replace 3100 with AAA, OAA, E&P-era if applicable)
| # | Account | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 3100 | AAA (Accumulated Adjustments Account) | |
| 3110 | OAA (Other Adjustments) | |
| 3120 | Previously taxed income (PTI) | rare |
| 3130 | Earnings & Profits (pre-S, if converted from C) | |

### Partnership (capital accounts by partner)
| # | Account | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 3100 | Partner A — capital | tax-basis method |
| 3110 | Partner B — capital | tax-basis method |

### LLC — single-member or taxed as C-corp (no par stock unless units certificated)
| # | Account | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 3060 | Member capital — `<member>` | every credit names its documented contribution/issuance (date + resolution) — see `scenarios/section-1244.md` on why bare equity credits leak |
| 3070 | Member distributions | contra-equity; closes to 3060 (or RE) at year-end |
| 3100 | Retained earnings | if taxed as C-corp |

An LLC taxed as a C-corp uses member capital/units, **not** common stock + APIC, unless it has actually certificated units — don't import corporate equity accounts the entity's own paper doesn't support. A disregarded SMLLC's full member equity here mirrors the parent's `1860 Investment` account (`entities/disregarded.md` § two-tier equity model).

